// Strava API application — the template. Copy to `Strava.xcconfig` and fill in the secret:
//
//     cd ios && cp Strava.example.xcconfig Strava.xcconfig
//
// `Strava.xcconfig` is GITIGNORED and must stay that way: this repository is public, and
// STRAVA_CLIENT_SECRET is the one value here that is actually a secret. `xcodegen generate`
// creates the copy for you if it is missing, so a fresh clone builds with no Strava
// credentials at all — the app then reports "No Strava application configured" on the
// Import screen and everything else works exactly as before.
//
// Where these come from: https://www.strava.com/settings/api
//   Application name              CleanJibe
//   Category                      Performance analysis
//   Website                       https://cleanjibe.org
//   Authorization Callback Domain cleanjibe.org
//
// The callback domain is the load-bearing one. Strava validates the redirect against it and
// refuses anything whose host is not that domain — custom schemes included — which is why
// the redirect below is an https URL on our own site. `web/strava/callback/index.html` is a
// static page whose only job is to forward the `code` and `state` to `cleanjibe://strava`,
// where ASWebAuthenticationSession is waiting. Change one of the two and you must change
// the other, plus the `cleanjibe` entry in project.yml's CFBundleURLTypes.

// Public by construction: it travels in every authorize URL.
STRAVA_CLIENT_ID = 279015

// SECRET. Copy it from the "My API Application" page. Never commit the file that holds it.
STRAVA_CLIENT_SECRET =

// Must match the Authorization Callback Domain above. Leave it as it is unless the Strava
// application is re-registered against a different domain.
//
// `//` inside a value starts a comment in an xcconfig, so the scheme separator has to be
// spelled through a variable — `SLASH` below is that trick, and it is why this line looks
// the way it does.
SLASH = /
STRAVA_REDIRECT_URI = https:$(SLASH)$(SLASH)cleanjibe.org/strava/callback
